# HomeKit Characteristics Implementation Verification

## Overview
This rule defines the requirements for implementing HomeKit characteristics in the OpenHAB HomeKit binding.

## Author
Karel Goderis

## Requirements

### 0. Source Information
Cross-reference with the file @CharacteristicDefinitions.ts 
Every file verified needs to be "touched" so that its last modified date gets updated

### 1. Base Class Selection
- For `Formats.FLOAT` → Use `HomekitFloatCharacteristic`
- For `Formats.UINT8`, `Formats.UINT16`, `Formats.UINT32`, `Formats.INT` → Use `HomekitIntegerCharacteristic`
- For `Formats.BOOL` → Use `HomekitBooleanCharacteristic`
- For `Formats.STRING` → Use `HomekitStringCharacteristic`
- For `Formats.TLV8` → Use `HomekitTLV8Characteristic`
- For `Formats.DATA` → Use `HomekitDataCharacteristic`
- For characteristics with `validValues` field and `format: Formats.UINT8` → Use `HomekitEnumCharacteristic`

### 2. Class Structure
- Place in `src/main/java/org/openhab/io/homekit/library/characteristic/`
- Annotate with `@HomekitCharacteristicType` including:
  - `type`: UUID from HAP specification
  - `name`: Name from HAP specification
  - `tag`: camelCase version of name
- Implement value range, step, and unit as per HAP specification
- For enum characteristics, define an enum class with valid values
- Classes using `HomekitEnumCharacteristic` should implement a custom enum instead of constants
- if `validValues` is present, then the specific enum in the class can not have more options than values in `validValues`. The names of the enum values are mentioned in the file @CharacteristicDefinitions.ts 
- There is not need to create static fields like MIN_VALUE, MAX_VALUE or UNIT. Directly use them in the constructor calls
- "Units" should be "celcius" ,"percentage", "arcdegrees", "lux", "seconds" and not a symbol like "C", "%",...
 - Implement isAllowedValue for value range validation
 - For enum characteristics, implement getAllowedValues
 - Implement required methods for value conversion and validation
 - Use proper null safety annotations
 - Use with() methods in constructors
 - Cross-check the UUID and name with what is in https://raw.githubusercontent.com/homebridge/HAP-NodeJS/4eb81ee52934b5f312ef470440a0947542b6fd5b/src/lib/definitions/CharacteristicDefinitions.ts
 - Remove @override methods like toEventJson, toValueJson, ... that are redundant
 - Classes inheriting from HomekitEnumCharacteristic should implement a setValue() method taking the specific enum as input parameter. This setValue method should handle any exceptions and throw any exception itself

### 3. Documentation
- Add Javadoc comment referencing the HAP specification in general to https://developer.apple.com/documentation/HomeKit (do not use a specific or non-existing url)
- Remove any references to homebridge.io
- Include characteristic description and purpose
- Include an author field : "Karel Goderis"

### 4. Code Quality
- Remove unnecessary `@Override` methods that only call `super()`
- Implement required methods for value conversion and validation
- Use proper null safety annotations (`@NonNullByDefault`)
- Follow Java naming conventions
- Import all necessary classes and do not use fully qualified classnames 

### 5. Permissions
- Set permissions according to HAP specification:
  - `pairedRead`: Based on `Perms.PAIRED_READ`
  - `pairedWrite`: Based on `Perms.PAIRED_WRITE`
  - `events`: Based on `Perms.NOTIFY`

### 6. Value Validation
- Implement `isAllowedValue` for value range validation
- For enum characteristics, implement `getAllowedValues`
- Handle null values appropriately

## Example Implementation
```java
/**
 * HomeKit Characteristic Name.
 * This characteristic represents [description].
 *
 * @author Karel Goderis - Initial Contribution
 */
@HomekitCharacteristicType(type = "UUID", name = "Name", tag = "camelCaseName")
@NonNullByDefault
public class HomekitCharacteristicName extends HomekitBaseCharacteristic {
    public HomekitCharacteristicName(HomekitService service, HomekitEventManager eventManager, long instanceId) {
        super(service, eventManager);
        withInstanceId(instanceId)
            .withPairedRead(true)
            .withPairedWrite(false)
            .withEvents(true)
            .withDescription("Description");
    }
}
```

## Verification Checklist
- [ ] UUID matches HAP specification
- [ ] Name matches HAP specification
- [ ] Base class matches format
- [ ] Permissions match HAP specification
- [ ] Documentation references HAP specification
- [ ] No homebridge.io references
- [ ] No unnecessary overrides
- [ ] Proper null safety
- [ ] Value validation implemented
- [ ] Enum values defined if required
